The analog baseline (ccf/models/analog.py) and the scoring rules
(ccf/hindcast.py) reproduce the method and the proper-score definitions of
hydrohistorian.com's curtailment outlook and skill module, which are
otherwise proprietary. They are released here under Apache-2.0 by their
author so that any contributed model is scored by the same rules the site
scores by.

The call truth table and the Division 1 bulk release this code reads are
published by hydrohistorian.com from public records of the Colorado
Division of Water Resources. SNOTEL data are from the USDA NRCS Air and
Water Database (public domain).
